# Living auction house (m7): the AuctionHouseBot seller lists materials and gear (write-confs); Arpg.AH.AffixShare % of its
# green-epic gear listings roll affixes at the item's required-level tier + Arpg.AH.TierOffset (-1), buyout = sell formula x
# Arpg.AH.AffixMarkup (4), never below the seller's own price. `.arpg test ah` runs the hook on one listing (share forced).

# A level-18ish green (2317): 1-2 affixes; the buyout rises above the stand-in price.
> .arpg test ah 2317
? ok ah item=2317 level=\d+ affixes=[12] base=(\d+) buyout=\d+ bid=\d+
# A blue (1489): 2-3 affixes.
> .arpg test ah 1489
? affixes=[23]\b
# Materials and stock random-stat items are left plain.
> .arpg test ah 2589
? affixes=0 .*\(not gear\)
